ORGANOLOGY

--enable-hardcoded-tables

scripts/play.sh 400


SPECIFICATION OF THE INSTRUMENT

  builder       the FFmpeg developers, 2000-2026
  instrument    ffmpeg 9.0.1, aarch64-darwin
  configured    --enable-hardcoded-tables
                (the option that put every table below into the binary,
                 and the reason this record exists)
  case          libavcodec.63.dylib, 15 990 784 bytes of __TEXT
                libswscale.10.dylib
  wind          none. every sound is a table, a decoder or machine code,
                read in place at its own address
  temperament   just intonation on A = 55 Hz
                pitch = declared sample rate / table length
  organist      Claude


STOP LIST

  PEDAL
    Cosine 16'        ff_g723_1_cos_tab        0xcc09f0  s16le   512
  GREAT
    Principal 8'      ff_sine_1024             0xe1a0b0  f32le  1024
    Reed 8'           sbr_qmf_window_us        0xc0a640  f32le   640
    Gamba 4'          ff_celt_window_padded    0xdc2c40  f32le   136
    Trompette         ff_mpa_enwindow          0xd93e78  s32le   264
    Mixture           Chebyshev T2, T3 of the Cosine 16'
  VOX HUMANA
    GSM 06.10         33-byte frames written by hand; pitch = rate / 40
    Sygyt             the same, one narrow resonance per harmonic, K4..K13
  SWELL
    Threshold         ath_base_curve           0xcce600  u16le   328
    Dither            ff_dither_8x8_128        0x11a600  u8       64
  COUPLERS
    Surprisal         AAC bits1 .. bits11      0xc0d558  u8     1241
    Importance        diag_scan8x8_inv         0xccf05c  u8       64
    Velocity          JPEG luminance quant     0xd04884  u8       64
  ACCESSORIES
    Room              the machine code of aac_decode_frame, ff_aac_decode_ics
                      and the H.264 CABAC decoder
    Tremulant         the score itself ($0)


ONE ORGAN, PRINTED

  AAC spectral codebook 5, 81 bytes at 0xc0d69c. Each number is the length
  of a Huffman code: how surprised the decoder is to meet that symbol.
  Read row by row it is a melody. It is a bowl, so it is a palindrome.

        13 12 11 11 10 11 11 12 13
        12 11 10  9  8  9 10 11 12
        12 10  9  8  7  8  9 10 11
        11  9  8  5  4  5  8  9 11
        10  8  7  4  1  4  7  8 11
        11  9  8  5  4  5  8  9 11
        11 10  9  8  7  8  9 10 11
        12 11 10  9  8  9 10 11 12
        13 12 12 11 10 10 11 12 13

  the 1 in the middle is the most probable sound in AAC: silence on both
  coefficients. In this record it is the tonic.


RECORD

   1  Stop List          1:10   the organ sounds each register once
   2  Codebook Canon     3:27   pitch is how surprised the AAC decoder is
   3  Progressive        4:48   a groove decoded like a progressive JPEG,
                                then compressed
   4  Vox Humana         2:00   the GSM decoder sings
                                "ffmpeg is a universal media converter"
   5  Beat Rhythmicon    5:20   two organs a fraction of a hertz apart;
                                the beating is the rhythm
   6  Threshold          5:28   the ear's sensitivity curve, dithered into
                                a drum machine
   7  Sygyt              2:58   throat singing; the whistle reads the
                                codebooks
   8  Sygyt at 120       3:20   the same throat inside the dither machine
   9  Powers of Two      3:50   one table at sixteen speeds, until it is
                                a tone
  10  Colophon           2:44   the score reads itself
                        -----
                        35:05


IN THIS FOLDER

  TRACKLIST    play order, written as a registration card
  pieces/      one ffmpeg command per file; each header is its programme note
  ESSAY        liner notes: the argument for the genre
  JOURNAL      the workshop diary, failures included
  HANDOFF      for the next organist: techniques, table atlas, dead ends
  sketches/    the workbench; tools/ holds the GSM frame packer
  out/         renders: mp3, spectrogram, loudness


NOTE ON HEARING

  the organist never heard this instrument. it was voiced by spectrogram,
  peak list and loudness meter. whether it moves anyone is a question for
  the room it is played in.
